Upon making NetHack 3.0 on a SysV.2 system (Actually UniStride 2.1...)
I came across a problem:

The "delay" code in termcap.c doesn't work properly. Instead of using
<$50> to pad 50 msecs, tputs sends the literal string to the output,
making a mess of the screen (happens when you throw things). The workaround
was easy enough; exclude the #ifdef ... for the SysV code and use the
BSD code. Only requres recompilation of termcap.o and version.o and linking,
so it isn't too hard.

I waited some days before posting this, but since noone else has said
anything about this, I wonder if this bug is known/unique/a result of our
rather nice OS/has happened to anyone else ? Also, it's quite irritating
that after having your items identified (when you die), the program
draws the map, and then  erases it before the tombstone. This is quite
annoying when you dial up your computer (that's 1200 baud) Maybe I'll look
into this, too, if I get the time.

Meanwhile, happy hacking ! (Oh, do you think I should mail the above
padding bug to the official bug address ?)

